# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# refund-api environment variables
#
# DATA RESIDENCY — MANDATORY constraints (spec 007, CLAUDE.md):
#   1. EU region: this service MUST be deployed to an EU region only.
#      Production target: Railway EU (europe-west4), matching estimai-api/
#      notify-api's railway.json — wired by T19. No reimbursement data
#      (financial figures, receipt PII) may be stored outside the EU.
#   2. No body logging: request/response bodies (expense line motivations,
#      amounts, receipt metadata) must NEVER appear in application logs.
#      hono/logger is configured to emit method+path+status only (see
#      src/index.ts / src/lib/logger.ts). Do NOT add any logger that includes
#      body, query parameters with content, or the Prisma 'query' log level.
#
# T4 (this bootstrap) only wires identity verification (ADR-0005/0010). Later
# tasks add more required vars to this file — see the per-var notes below.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local: point at the compose Postgres (host port 5435, 'refund' database).
# Production (Railway): use the Railway-provisioned Postgres URL (Railway EU).
# T5 adds the first migration (0001_init) — this DB is otherwise empty until
# `bun run db:migrate` is run after that schema lands.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5435/refund

# ─── CORS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of allowed origins (no wildcards).
# Must include the shell origin(s) for each environment — refund-ui is a
# federated remote reached through the shell (ADR-0006), not called directly.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000

# ─── Auth (JWT resource-server verification) ─────────────────────────────────
# auth service JWKS endpoint — used by jwtMiddleware to verify RS256 tokens.
# Both values are required; the service will refuse to start if either is missing.
#
# IMPORTANT: use /auth/jwks (better-auth's built-in JWKS endpoint) NOT
# /.well-known/jwks.json — the latter serves the env-var key (kid:
# operai-auth-rs256-v1) which is a DIFFERENT key from the one better-auth's
# jwt plugin uses (stored in the jwks table, dynamic kid). The /auth/token
# endpoint signs with the DB keypair, so refund-api must verify against
# /auth/jwks.
AUTH_JWKS_URL=http://localhost:3001/auth/jwks
AUTH_ISSUER=http://localhost:3001

# Suite-wide JWT audience (ADR-0010). Must exactly match the `audience` claim
# the auth service stamps via its jwt plugin's definePayload hook — a mismatch
# (or a token that predates the claim) is rejected with 401. Treat this as a
# single suite-wide constant, documented identically in auth/.env.example and
# every resource server's .env.example (estimai-api, notify-api, refund-api).
AUTH_AUDIENCE=operai-suite

# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8082 — estimai-api is 8080, notify-api is 8081 (CLAUDE.md § Resource backends).
PORT=8082
NODE_ENV=development

# ─── Not yet wired (added by later tasks — do not add manually) ──────────────
# T6  — no new env var (calls `auth GET /authz/resolve`, forwarding the
#        caller's own Bearer token; no separate credential).
# T9  — REFUND_S3_ENDPOINT / REFUND_S3_REGION / REFUND_S3_BUCKET /
#        REFUND_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID / REFUND_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY (EU-region
#        object storage for receipt attachments; REFUND_S3_REGION validated
#        against an EU allowlist at startup).
# T13 — NOTIFY_INTERNAL_TOKEN (shared with auth/notify-api, ADR-0011 pattern)
#        + the notify-api base URL, for the decision→notification push.
